WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.600
With just weeks to go before the film's release,
a second trailer for Halloween has arrived

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:05.680
to scare us all.

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:10.700
Set 40 years after Michael Myers first terrorized
the town of Haddonfield, the new film will

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.800
ignore every one of the series' sequels.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:17.460
That means no cults, no psychic visions, and
none of the mythology that made Michael a

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.220
brother to Jamie Lee Curtis' Laurie Strode.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:25.360
Despite this axing of the canon, the new movie
was made in cooperation with John Carpenter,

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:28.340
the original movie's director, co-writer,
and composer.

00:00:28.429 --> 00:00:33.700
So Halloween isn't totally rejecting its franchise
instead, it's reinterpreting it in an exciting

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.200
way.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:38.300
The new trailer is packed with interesting
details and references that you might not

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.660
have seen at first glance.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.240
Let's shine a light on the little things you
may have missed.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:44.000
Close encounter

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:48.800
From the marketing, it's clear the new Halloween
is getting back to the series' roots.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.770
The trailer's first shot follows two kids
trick-or-treating, trying to decide which

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:54.560
house to plunder for candy next.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:59.400
They literally run into a tall, rigid figure
in a black jumpsuit who barely reacts to them.

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.340
The kids scurry away, and Michael goes on
about his murderous business.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:08.500
The shot mirrors a daytime scene from the
1978 film, when one of the boys bullying Tommy

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.060
Doyle runs away from school only to almost
plow into Michael.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:16.800
It's a reference to the original that also
serves to deepen our understanding of Michael.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.180
Even if you bump right into him, nothing bothers
this killing machine.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.100
Hack o'lantern

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:26.860
The jack o'lantern is synonymous with Halloween
both the holiday, and the original film.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:30.730
They can be seen everywhere as Michael stalks
the streets of Haddonfield, but they're more

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:31.880
than just set dressing.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:34.170
They also seem to give Michael some ideas.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:38.880
At one point in the trailer, a car door opens
to reveal a crude jack o'lantern made from

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:43.750
a flayed human face on what appears to be
a dead cop's lap, illuminated from the inside

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:44.660
by a flashlight.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.040
Why Michael would stop in the middle of his
killing spree for some morbid arts and crafts

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:52.000
is a mystery, but you can't deny it's an amazing
gore moment.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.500
If they put that in the trailer, we can't
wait to see what's in the movie.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.140
Silver Shamrock

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:02.500
The third Halloween movie, Season of the Witch,
is the only entry in the series not to feature

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:03.400
Michael Myers.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:08.680
A standalone story about haunted novelty masks,
the movie was a failed effort to turn the

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.400
Halloween series into an anthology.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:15.040
But despite existing outside of Michael's
story, the threequel still gets a shout-out

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:15.860
in this trailer.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:20.390
As Laurie runs around like a madwoman, waving
a gun around and shouting people off the streets,

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:24.650
we see three children run by wearing three
different masks: A witch, a skeleton, and

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:26.060
a jack o'lantern.

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:30.340
These three masks are recognizable as the
ones made by Halloween III's Silver Shamrock

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:33.480
company cursed objects that killed the people
wearing them.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:37.900
So while most of the continuity may be done
for, Silver Shamrock still lives on.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.060
You'll never get that theme song out of your
head.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:46.480
"It's four days till halloween halloween halloween,
it's four days til halloween, Silll-verrr

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:47.060
shamrock!"

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:48.980
Castle doctrine

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:53.990
The new film's Laurie has spent her adult
life preparing for the return of Michael Myers,

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:58.000
but despite her dedication to survivalism,
she also managed to have a family.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:02.860
In the new trailer, she chastises her daughter
Karen for being lax about security, which

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:04.100
Karen dismisses.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.380
She even seems to think her mom is crazy.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.760
"You have no security system, Karen."

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:10.370
"Mom — you need help."

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.920
As the trailer demonstrates, Laurie really
needs no help.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:17.290
We've already seen her out in the woods practicing
her target shooting, and keeping an underground

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:18.960
bunker stocked with supplies.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:24.300
This trailer reveals more of her In-Case-of-Michael
setup, including a hidden gun cabinet, floodlights

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:28.800
on her roof, and a panic room door that slams
down as she prepares for a confrontation.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:33.160
She's been waiting for this fight for years,
and while she seems capable of getting vengeance,

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:35.640
hopefully Michael doesn't take her with him
when he goes.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:37.320
Core work

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:42.840
One of the most memorable moments in the original
Halloween occurs as Laurie sits exhausted,

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:45.240
with Michael seemingly dead on the floor behind
her.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:49.880
It's a tension-relieving moment until Michael
suddenly sits bolt upright, looking completely

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:50.380
unharmed.

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:55.320
It's not a corny jump scare, either he sits
up in silence, moving in a completely stiff,

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:56.990
frighteningly unnatural way.

00:03:56.990 --> 00:03:59.760
He doesn't move like a man sporting fresh
stab wounds.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:03.940
The trailer shows the new movie bringing back
that maneuver, with Michael doing the iconic

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:07.500
sit-up once again after Laurie knocks him
down some stairs.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:12.060
Even after 40 years, Michael's remarkable
core strength is apparently still intact.

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:13.460
His abs must be incredible.

